      "description": "Instructor of Agriculture | Human Resources | Southern Arkansas University Skip to main content Quick Links Calendar Directory mySAU Email: Student | Faculty Blackboard Course Schedule Library Give Tour Apply About Administration Accreditations Continuous Quality Improvement Consumer Information Financial Services Institutional Research Student Complaint Form Human Resources Mission and Vision Mulerider Mascot News Campus Map Faculty/Staff Resources Center for Excellence in Teaching & Learning Online Learning Physical Plant Request Staff Email Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Concurrent Enrollment Graduate Admissions International Admissions Tuition and Fees Cost Calculator Scholarships Financial Aid Orientation (BAM) Academics Colleges & Departments Business Education & Human Performance Liberal & Performing Arts Science & Engineering Honors Graduate Studies Majors and Degrees General Education Professional License Disclosure Academic Calendar Catalogs Resources Academic Advising Bookstore Magale Library Registrar Student Support Services Writing Center Online Learning Blackboard mySAU Course Schedules LiveText Student Email Final Exam Schedule Campus Life Students Club Sports Greek Life Let’s Talk Webcast Student Conduct Student Handbook Track the Ride Housing Application Costs Amenities Housing Options What to Bring Facilities Bookstore Campus Dining Campus Map Mulerider Activity Center Reynolds Center Story Arena Facilities Rental Physical Plant Request Mulerider Express Career Services Counseling Center University Health Services Athletics Alumni & Friends Alumni Association Office of Development Foundation The Stater Magazine A-Z Index Calendar Give Directory Apply Now Office of Human Resources About New Hires New Employee Orientation Policies Jobs Adminstrative Positions Faculty Positions Staff Positions Part-time Forms Whole Health Holiday Schedule Summer Staff Schedule Staff Awards Spirit of SAU Awards Valuing People Awards Whitehead Staff Excellence Awards Contact You are here: Home / Employment Opportunities / Instructor of Agriculture Instructor of Agriculture Southern Arkansas University’s College of Science and Engineering is accepting applications for an Instructor of Agriculture position. The successful candidate will teach introductory-level plant science courses and labs, as well as related courses in plant science such as greenhouse management. Additional teaching responsibilities may include courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Southern Arkansas University offers competitive salaries commensurate with experience as well as an excellent fringe benefits package. Duties: Teach upper- and lower-division plant science courses as well as courses in the candidate’s area of expertise; prepare, organize, supervise, and deliver hands-on learning labs that support classroom curriculum; engage in recruitment, retention, and other duties as assigned. The teaching load is expected to average 15 credit hours per semester Qualifications: Master’s degree in an agriculture field required; university teaching experience preferred; ability to teach undergraduate students; excellent communication skills; ability to work well with others; have a strong desire to interact with students both inside and outside the classroom All SAU faculty and staff demonstrate a commitment to the value of all members of the SAU community, to excellence in interpersonal behaviors, and effective collaboration with colleagues. Joining the SAU family requires a commitment to our culture of Continuous Quality Improvement. Applicants should send a letter of application, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, transcripts, and the names and telephone numbers of three (3) references to hr@saumag.edu or to the Office of Human Resources, Southern Arkansas University, 100 E. University, MSC 9288, Magnolia, AR 71753. Non-listed references may be contacted. AA/EOE. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Posted: June 24, 2026 Apply Online Contact Us Office of Human Resources 100 E. University OVR 115 Magnolia, AR 71753 Office (870) 235-4008 Fax (870) 235-5050 Staff Tammy  Sims Tammy  Sims Human Resources Manager Roger Giles Roger Giles Vice President for Administration & General Counsel Micah Williams Micah Williams Administrative Support Specialist Jennifer Richardson Jennifer Richardson Administrative Specialist III Important Links Fringe Benefits Brochure Payroll & Employee Benefits Health Insurance Plan Document Health Insurance Summary of Benefits and Coverage ABCBS - Machine-Readable Files SAU Tech Employment Opportunities Social Security Administration Student Employment Office Schools & Colleges Business Education & Human Performance Liberal & Performing Arts Science & Engineering Honors College Graduate Studies Quick Links Scholarships & Financial Aid Jobs @ SAU Course Schedules Transcript Request Beyond the Campus Store Bookstore Transferring to SAU Finals Schedule Title IX Campus Emergency Alerts Social Calendar of Events Make a Gift Photos.SAUmag.edu Apply Now Southern Arkansas University is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission . All Rights Reserved. 100 E. University , Magnolia , Arkansas 71753-5000 Telephone: (870) 235-4000 Online Privacy"
