      "description": "Assistant Professor of Human Performance & Sports Sciences - Exercise Science (Strength & Conditioning) | Human Resources | Southern Arkansas University Skip to main content Quick Links Calendar Directory mySAU Email: Student | Faculty Blackboard Course Schedule Library Give Tour Apply About Administration Accreditations Continuous Quality Improvement Consumer Information Financial Services Institutional Research Student Complaint Form Human Resources Mission and Vision Mulerider Mascot News Campus Map Faculty/Staff Resources Center for Excellence in Teaching & Learning Online Learning Physical Plant Request Staff Email Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Concurrent Enrollment Graduate Admissions International Admissions Tuition and Fees Cost Calculator Scholarships Financial Aid Orientation (BAM) Academics Colleges & Departments Business Education & Human Performance Liberal & Performing Arts Science & Engineering Honors Graduate Studies Majors and Degrees General Education Professional License Disclosure Academic Calendar Catalogs Resources Academic Advising Bookstore Magale Library Registrar Student Support Services Writing Center Online Learning Blackboard mySAU Course Schedules LiveText Student Email Final Exam Schedule Campus Life Students Club Sports Greek Life Let’s Talk Webcast Student Conduct Student Handbook Track the Ride Housing Application Costs Amenities Housing Options What to Bring Facilities Bookstore Campus Dining Campus Map Mulerider Activity Center Reynolds Center Story Arena Facilities Rental Physical Plant Request Mulerider Express Career Services Counseling Center University Health Services Athletics Alumni & Friends Alumni Association Office of Development Foundation The Stater Magazine A-Z Index Calendar Give Directory Apply Now Office of Human Resources About New Hires New Employee Orientation Policies Jobs Adminstrative Positions Faculty Positions Staff Positions Part-time Forms Whole Health Holiday Schedule Summer Staff Schedule Staff Awards Spirit of SAU Awards Valuing People Awards Whitehead Staff Excellence Awards Contact You are here: Home / Employment Opportunities / Assistant Professor of Human Performance & Sports Sciences – Exercise Science (Strength & Conditioning) Assistant Professor of Human Performance & Sports Sciences – Exercise Science (Strength & Conditioning) Southern Arkansas University is accepting applications for a 9-month Assistant or Associate Professor, tenure-track position in Exercise Science with an emphasis in Strength & Conditioning. The start date for this position is August 1, 2026. The Department of Human Performance and Sport Sciences, one of the largest at Southern Arkansas University, offers undergraduate degrees in exercise science, sports management, and K-12 physical education, as well as a graduate degree in kinesiology with an emphasis in sport coaching. The dynamic exercise science program, among the fastest-growing majors on campus, currently serves over 155 students across two tracks: pre-professional, which prepares students for graduate programs in fields such as physical therapy, athletic training, and occupational therapy, and strength and conditioning, which equips students for careers in fitness and sports performance. Duties: teach a full-time course load in the exercise science program using a student-centered approach while delivering instruction through both face-to-face and online modalities; advise and mentor undergraduate exercise science students; engage in scholarly activities, such as research, publications, and presentations, and contributing to university, department, and community service through committees, other initiatives, and other duties as assigned. Qualifications: must hold an earned doctorate in exercise science or a closely related field, though those who are ABD may be considered with the expectation of degree completion by the start date; should demonstrate the ability to deliver a wide range of undergraduate exercise science courses and a commitment to developing or refining curricula to enhance program offerings; dedication to supporting diverse student populations and using data for continuous program improvement is essential; demonstrate a record of or potential for scholarly activity including publications, presentations, or securing external funding; demonstrate the ability to collaborate effectively within the department to strengthen the undergraduate program; familiarity with standards set by professional organizations like the American College of Sports Medicine (ACSM), National Strength and Conditioning Association (via NSCA), or related bodies required. Preference will be given to candidates with professional credentialing through nationally recognized organizations such as ACSM, NSCA, CSCCa, or NASM. A valid CPR/First Aid/AED certification or the ability to obtain certification prior to the start date is also preferred. Experience teaching courses such as strength and conditioning, trends in strength and conditioning, human anatomy and physiology, therapeutic exercise, applied statistics, and/or instrumentation and physiological assessment are highly desirable. All SAU faculty and staff demonstrate a commitment to the value of all members of the SAU community, to excellence in interpersonal behaviors, and effective collaboration with colleagues. Joining the SAU family requires a commitment to our culture of Continuous Quality Improvement. Southern Arkansas University is a public comprehensive regional university located in the city of Magnolia, located in southwest Arkansas. SAU is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. More information is available at www.saumag.edu Interested candidates should send a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, transcripts, and the contact information of three (3) references to HR@saumag.edu or the Office of Human Resources, Southern Arkansas University, 100 E. University, MSC 9288, Magnolia, AR 71753. AA/EOE. Finalists for the position may have non-listed references contacted. Notification will be given to the finalist should a non-listed reference come from their current employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a qualified person has been identified for the position. Posted: May 5, 2026 Apply Online Contact Us Office of Human Resources 100 E. University OVR 115 Magnolia, AR 71753 Office (870) 235-4008 Fax (870) 235-5050 Staff Tammy  Sims Tammy  Sims Human Resources Manager Roger Giles Roger Giles Vice President for Administration & General Counsel Micah Williams Micah Williams Administrative Support Specialist Jennifer Richardson Jennifer Richardson Administrative Specialist III Important Links Fringe Benefits Brochure Payroll & Employee Benefits Health Insurance Plan Document Health Insurance Summary of Benefits and Coverage ABCBS - Machine-Readable Files SAU Tech Employment Opportunities Social Security Administration Student Employment Office Schools & Colleges Business Education & Human Performance Liberal & Performing Arts Science & Engineering Honors College Graduate Studies Quick Links Scholarships & Financial Aid Jobs @ SAU Course Schedules Transcript Request Beyond the Campus Store Bookstore Transferring to SAU Finals Schedule Title IX Campus Emergency Alerts Social Calendar of Events Make a Gift Photos.SAUmag.edu Apply Now Southern Arkansas University is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission . All Rights Reserved. 100 E. University , Magnolia , Arkansas 71753-5000 Telephone: (870) 235-4000 Online Privacy"
